/-! # When a 1-morphism of stacks in groupoids makes the source a gerbe over the target

Stacks 06P1 gives two equivalent readings of "`F : 𝒳 ⥤ 𝒴` makes `𝒳` a gerbe over `𝒴`" for a
1-morphism `F` of stacks in groupoids over a site `(𝒞, J)`:

1. replacing `F` by a factorization `F = F' ∘ a` through an equivalence `a` over `𝒞` with `F'`
   fibred in groupoids — such a factorization exists by Stacks 06N7 — the functor `F'` is a
   *gerbe over the site* `(𝒴, J𝒴)`, where `J𝒴` is the topology inherited from `(𝒞, J)`; this is
   `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsGerbe` (Stacks 06NZ);
2. two local conditions on `F` itself, phrased over coverings of `𝒞`: every object of `𝒴` is
   locally in the image of `F`, and every morphism of a fibre of `q` between `F`-images is
   locally an `F`-image; these two conditions are exactly `CategoryTheory.IsGerbeOver`
   (Stacks 06P2), whose two fields they are.

The reading (2) is the one the definition Stacks 06P2 is built on in this development, so what
06P1 adds is the passage between the two — between local conditions over coverings of `𝒞` and the
gerbe conditions over coverings of `𝒴`.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.locallyNonempty_iff_locally_essSurj`: clause (2)(a) of Stacks 06P1, the first
  field of `IsGerbeOver`, is `CategoryTheory.Functor.LocallyNonempty` for the inherited topology.
* `CategoryTheory.locallyConnected_iff_locally_full`: clause (2)(b), the second field of
  `IsGerbeOver`, is `CategoryTheory.Functor.LocallyConnected` for the inherited topology.
* `CategoryTheory.isGerbeOver_iff_locallyNonempty_locallyConnected`: the two together.
* `CategoryTheory.Functor.isGerbe_iff_isGerbeOver`: Stacks 06P1 for an `F` that is already fibred
  in groupoids, i.e. at the trivial factorization.
* `CategoryTheory.isGerbe_of_factorization_iff_isGerbeOver`: **Stacks 06P1**, at an arbitrary
  factorization.

## Implementation notes

The passage between coverings of `𝒴` and coverings of `𝒞` is
`CategoryTheory.Functor.IsInheritedTopology.mem_iff_functorPushforward`: a sieve on an object of
`𝒴` is `J𝒴`-covering exactly when its image sieve is `J`-covering. Going from a covering of `𝒞`
to one of `𝒴` is where a choice is made: for each arrow of the covering sieve one picks the
object of `𝒳` (respectively the pair of restrictions) that the local condition supplies, and the
covering of `𝒴` is generated by the `F`-images of those choices. Going the other way needs no
choice, only lifts along `F` and along `F ⋙ q` to move an object or a morphism from an arrow of
the pushforward sieve to the arrow of the original sieve it factors through.

`LocallyConnected` asks for two restrictions over *one and the same* object of `𝒴` together with
an isomorphism between them in the fibre, whereas clause (2)(b) asks for a commuting square
between two restrictions that need only lie over the same object of `𝒞`. Both directions of
`locallyConnected_iff_locally_full` reconcile this by choosing the two restrictions to be the
*same* object of `𝒳`, so that the isomorphism asked for is the identity: an object of `𝒳` which
restricts both `x` and `x'` is what "`x|_V ≅ x'|_V` in the fibre" asserts, since for a category
fibred in groupoids every morphism lying over a base morphism exhibits its source as a
restriction of its target.

Both directions also need `F` and `q` to be fibred in groupoids, and never the descent
conditions; the descent half of "stack in groupoids" enters only in
`Functor.isGerbe_iff_isGerbeOver`, where it is what Stacks 06NX consumes to produce the
`IsStackInGroupoids` conjunct of `IsGerbe`. This is why the two clause-level biconditionals are
stated for functors merely fibred in groupoids, matching the hypotheses `IsGerbeOver` itself
carries.

The universe of the index types in `IsStackInGroupoids` and `IsInheritedTopology` is fixed to
`max u₃ v₃`, the universe in which the family of *all* arrows of a sieve on `𝒴` lives:
`IsInheritedTopology` constrains a topology only through families, so it is at that universe that
it constrains every sieve.

The hypothesis that `𝒳'` is a stack in groupoids over `𝒞` is carried explicitly in
`isGerbe_of_factorization_iff_isGerbeOver`. The source obtains it from `𝒳` by Stacks 042X, which
is available here as
`CategoryTheory.BasedCategory.isFiberedInGroupoids_and_isStack_iff_of_equivalence` — stated for
`CategoryTheory.Functor.IsStack` (Stacks 026F) rather than for
`CategoryTheory.Functor.IsStackInGroupoids` (Stacks 02ZI), which are two different renderings of
"stack", so it does not discharge this hypothesis as it stands.
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory

universe v₁ v₂ v₃ v₄ u₁ u₂ u₃ u₄

namespace CategoryTheory

variable {𝒞 : Type u₁} {𝒳 : Type u₂} {𝒴 : Type u₃}
  [Category.{v₁} 𝒞] [Category.{v₂} 𝒳] [Category.{v₃} 𝒴]
  {q : 𝒴 ⥤ 𝒞} {F : 𝒳 ⥤ 𝒴} {J : GrothendieckTopology 𝒞} {J𝒴 : GrothendieckTopology 𝒴}

/-- A sieve generated by arrows lifting the members of a `J`-covering sieve is `J𝒴`-covering. -/
private theorem ofArrows_mem_of_isHomLift
    (hq : q.IsFiberedInGroupoids) (hJ𝒴 : Functor.IsInheritedTopology.{max u₃ v₃} q J J𝒴)
    {y : 𝒴} {S : Sieve (q.obj y)} (hS : S ∈ J (q.obj y))
    {z : (Σ V : 𝒞, {f : V ⟶ q.obj y // S.arrows f}) → 𝒴} {g : ∀ i, z i ⟶ y}
    (hg : ∀ i, q.IsHomLift i.2.val (g i)) : Sieve.ofArrows z g ∈ J𝒴 y := by
  refine (Functor.IsInheritedTopology.mem_iff_functorPushforward hq hJ𝒴 _).2
    (J.superset_covering ?_ hS)
  intro V f hf
  have := hg ⟨V, f, hf⟩
  refine ⟨z ⟨V, f, hf⟩, g ⟨V, f, hf⟩, eqToHom (IsHomLift.domain_eq q f (g ⟨V, f, hf⟩)).symm,
    (Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff _ _ _).2 ⟨⟨V, f, hf⟩, 𝟙 _, (Category.id_comp _).symm⟩, ?_⟩
  rw [IsHomLift.fac' q f (g ⟨V, f, hf⟩)]
  simp

/-- **Stacks 06P1 (2)(a)**, the first local condition, is `Functor.LocallyNonempty` of `F` for the
inherited topology: `𝒳` has an object over each member of some `J𝒴`-covering of an object `y` of
`𝒴` exactly when, for some `J`-covering of `q y`, along each member there is an object of `𝒳`
whose `F`-image maps to `y` over that member.

For the direction producing a covering of `𝒴`, the covering is generated by the `F`-images of the
chosen objects; the equation `f = eqToHom ≫ q (ψ i)` says that the given `J`-covering refines the
image of that family, which is what makes it `J𝒴`-covering. For the other direction an arrow of
the image sieve factors as `k ≫ q g` through an arrow `g` of the `J𝒴`-covering, and the object of
`𝒳` over the source of `g` is moved along `k` by a lift for `F ⋙ q`. -/
theorem locallyNonempty_iff_locally_essSurj
    (hq : q.IsFiberedInGroupoids) (hF : F.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (hJ𝒴 : Functor.IsInheritedTopology.{max u₃ v₃} q J J𝒴) :
    F.LocallyNonempty J𝒴 ↔
      ∀ {U : 𝒞} (y : 𝒴), q.obj y = U → ∃ S ∈ J U,
        ∀ ⦃V : 𝒞⦄ (f : V ⟶ U), S f → ∃ (x : 𝒳) (ψ : F.obj x ⟶ y), q.IsHomLift f ψ := by
  have hFq : (F ⋙ q).IsFiberedInGroupoids := Functor.IsFiberedInGroupoids.comp F q hF hq
  constructor
  · intro h U y hy
    subst hy
    obtain ⟨T, hT, hTne⟩ := h y
    refine ⟨Sieve.functorPushforward q T,
      (Functor.IsInheritedTopology.mem_iff_functorPushforward hq hJ𝒴 T).1 hT, ?_⟩
    rintro V f ⟨y₁, g, k, hg, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨⟨x, hx⟩⟩ := hTne g hg
    subst hx
    obtain ⟨x', χ, hχ⟩ := hFq.exists_lift k x rfl
    have := hχ
    have : q.IsHomLift k (F.map χ) := (Functor.isHomLift_comp_iff F q k χ).1 hχ
    have : q.IsHomLift (q.map g) g := IsHomLift.map (p := q) g
    exact ⟨x', F.map χ ≫ g, IsHomLift.comp q k (q.map g) (F.map χ) g⟩
  · intro h y
    obtain ⟨S, hS, hcov⟩ := h y rfl
    refine ⟨Sieve.ofArrows
        (fun i : Σ V : 𝒞, {f : V ⟶ q.obj y // S.arrows f} =>
          F.obj (hcov i.2.val i.2.property).choose)
        (fun i => (hcov i.2.val i.2.property).choose_spec.choose), ?_, ?_⟩
    · exact ofArrows_mem_of_isHomLift hq hJ𝒴 hS fun i =>
      (hcov i.2.val i.2.property).choose_spec.choose_spec
    · rintro Z k hk
      obtain ⟨i, c, rfl⟩ := (Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff _ _ _).1 hk
      obtain ⟨x', φ, hφ⟩ := hF.exists_lift c (hcov i.2.val i.2.property).choose rfl
      have := hφ
      exact ⟨⟨x', IsHomLift.domain_eq F c φ⟩⟩

/-- **Stacks 06P1 (2)(b)**, the second local condition, is `Functor.LocallyConnected` of `F` for
the inherited topology.

The two shapes are reconciled by taking the two restrictions to be one and the same object of
`𝒳`, so that the isomorphism `LocallyConnected` asks for is the identity. In the direction
producing clause (2)(b), the morphism `b` of a fibre of `q` is first replaced by a restriction
`β : x'' ⟶ x'` of `x'` along it, which puts `x` and `x''` over the same object of `𝒴`;
`LocallyConnected` applied to them supplies a covering of `𝒴` whose image sieve is the covering of
`𝒞` wanted, and along each of its members the composite `χ ≫ e.hom ≫ υ ≫ β` is a second
restriction of `x'` at the *same* object of `𝒳` that restricts `x`, so the commuting square holds
with `a` the identity. -/
theorem locallyConnected_iff_locally_full
    (hq : q.IsFiberedInGroupoids) (hF : F.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (hJ𝒴 : Functor.IsInheritedTopology.{max u₃ v₃} q J J𝒴) :
    F.LocallyConnected J𝒴 ↔
      ∀ {U : 𝒞} {x x' : 𝒳} (b : F.obj x ⟶ F.obj x'), q.IsHomLift (𝟙 U) b →
        ∃ S ∈ J U, ∀ ⦃V : 𝒞⦄ (f : V ⟶ U), S f →
          ∃ (x₁ x₁' : 𝒳) (ξ : x₁ ⟶ x) (ξ' : x₁' ⟶ x') (a : x₁ ⟶ x₁'),
            (F ⋙ q).IsHomLift f ξ ∧ (F ⋙ q).IsHomLift f ξ' ∧ (F ⋙ q).IsHomLift (𝟙 V) a ∧
              F.map a ≫ F.map ξ' = F.map ξ ≫ b := by
  have hFq : (F ⋙ q).IsFiberedInGroupoids := Functor.IsFiberedInGroupoids.comp F q hF hq
  constructor
  · intro h U x x' b hb
    have := hb
    have hU : q.obj (F.obj x) = U := IsHomLift.domain_eq q (𝟙 U) b
    subst hU
    obtain ⟨x'', β, hβ⟩ := hF.exists_lift b x' rfl
    have := hβ
    have hd : F.obj x'' = F.obj x := IsHomLift.domain_eq F b β
    obtain ⟨T, hT, hTcov⟩ := h x x'' rfl hd
    refine ⟨Sieve.functorPushforward q T,
      (Functor.IsInheritedTopology.mem_iff_functorPushforward hq hJ𝒴 T).1 hT, ?_⟩
    rintro V f ⟨y₁, g, k, hg, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨x₁, x₁'', ξ₁, υ, e, hξ₁, hυ, he⟩ := hTcov g hg
    have := hξ₁; have := hυ; have := he
    have hd₀ : F.obj x₁ = y₁ := IsHomLift.domain_eq F g ξ₁
    obtain ⟨x₂, χ, hχ⟩ := hFq.exists_lift k x₁ (congrArg q.obj hd₀)
    have := hχ
    have hgq : q.IsHomLift (q.map g) g := IsHomLift.map (p := q) g
    have hξ₁q : (F ⋙ q).IsHomLift (q.map g) ξ₁ := IsHomLift.comp_functor F q (q.map g) g ξ₁
    have hυq : (F ⋙ q).IsHomLift (q.map g) υ := IsHomLift.comp_functor F q (q.map g) g υ
    have hidy : q.IsHomLift (𝟙 (q.obj y₁)) (𝟙 y₁) := IsHomLift.id rfl
    have heq : (F ⋙ q).IsHomLift (𝟙 (q.obj y₁)) e.hom :=
      IsHomLift.comp_functor F q (𝟙 (q.obj y₁)) (𝟙 y₁) e.hom
    have hβq : (F ⋙ q).IsHomLift (𝟙 (q.obj (F.obj x))) β :=
      IsHomLift.comp_functor F q (𝟙 (q.obj (F.obj x))) b β
    have h1 : (F ⋙ q).IsHomLift (q.map g) (υ ≫ β) := by
      simpa using IsHomLift.comp (F ⋙ q) (q.map g) (𝟙 (q.obj (F.obj x))) υ β
    have h2 : (F ⋙ q).IsHomLift (q.map g) (e.hom ≫ υ ≫ β) := by
      simpa using IsHomLift.comp (F ⋙ q) (𝟙 (q.obj y₁)) (q.map g) e.hom (υ ≫ β)
    refine ⟨x₂, x₂, χ ≫ ξ₁, χ ≫ e.hom ≫ υ ≫ β, 𝟙 x₂,
      IsHomLift.comp (F ⋙ q) k (q.map g) χ ξ₁,
      IsHomLift.comp (F ⋙ q) k (q.map g) χ (e.hom ≫ υ ≫ β),
      IsHomLift.id (IsHomLift.domain_eq (F ⋙ q) k χ), ?_⟩
    have hsq : F.map e.hom ≫ F.map υ ≫ F.map β = F.map ξ₁ ≫ b := by
      rw [IsHomLift.fac' F (𝟙 y₁) e.hom, IsHomLift.fac' F g υ, IsHomLift.fac' F b β,
        IsHomLift.fac' F g ξ₁]
      simp
    simp only [F.map_id, F.map_comp, Category.id_comp, Category.assoc]
    rw [hsq]
  · intro h y x x' hx hx'
    subst hx
    have hb : q.IsHomLift (𝟙 (q.obj (F.obj x))) (eqToHom hx'.symm : F.obj x ⟶ F.obj x') :=
      IsHomLift.of_fac' q (𝟙 _) _ rfl (congrArg q.obj hx') (by simp [eqToHom_map])
    obtain ⟨S, hS, hcov⟩ := h (x := x) (x' := x') (eqToHom hx'.symm) hb
    have hdata : ∀ i : Σ V : 𝒞, {f : V ⟶ q.obj (F.obj x) // S.arrows f},
        ∃ (x₁ x₁' : 𝒳) (ξ : x₁ ⟶ x) (ξ' : x₁' ⟶ x') (a : x₁ ⟶ x₁'),
          (F ⋙ q).IsHomLift i.2.val ξ ∧ (F ⋙ q).IsHomLift i.2.val ξ' ∧
            (F ⋙ q).IsHomLift (𝟙 i.1) a ∧
            F.map a ≫ F.map ξ' = F.map ξ ≫ (eqToHom hx'.symm : F.obj x ⟶ F.obj x') :=
      fun i => hcov i.2.val i.2.property
    choose X1 X1' ξ ξ' a hξ hξ' ha hsq using hdata
    refine ⟨Sieve.ofArrows (fun i => F.obj (X1 i)) (fun i => F.map (ξ i)), ?_, ?_⟩
    · exact ofArrows_mem_of_isHomLift hq hJ𝒴 hS fun i =>
        (Functor.isHomLift_comp_iff F q i.2.val (ξ i)).1 (hξ i)
    · rintro Z k hk
      obtain ⟨i, c, rfl⟩ := (Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff _ _ _).1 hk
      obtain ⟨x₂, χ, hχ⟩ := hF.exists_lift c (X1 i) rfl
      have := hχ
      have hZ : F.obj x₂ = Z := IsHomLift.domain_eq F c χ
      have hmapξ : F.IsHomLift (F.map (ξ i)) (ξ i) := IsHomLift.map (p := F) (ξ i)
      refine ⟨x₂, x₂, χ ≫ ξ i, χ ≫ a i ≫ ξ' i, Iso.refl x₂,
        IsHomLift.comp F c (F.map (ξ i)) χ (ξ i), ?_, IsHomLift.id hZ⟩
      refine IsHomLift.of_fac' F (c ≫ F.map (ξ i)) (χ ≫ a i ≫ ξ' i) hZ hx' ?_
      simp only [F.map_comp, Category.assoc]
      rw [hsq i, IsHomLift.fac' F c χ]
      simp

/-- Clause (2) of Stacks 06P1 — that is, `CategoryTheory.IsGerbeOver` — is being locally nonempty
and locally connected over the inherited topology, for an `F` fibred in groupoids over a `q`
fibred in groupoids. The two fibredness fields of `IsGerbeOver` are the hypotheses `hq` and their
composite, so the biconditional is the conjunction of the two clause-level ones. -/
theorem isGerbeOver_iff_locallyNonempty_locallyConnected
    (hq : q.IsFiberedInGroupoids) (hF : F.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (hJ𝒴 : Functor.IsInheritedTopology.{max u₃ v₃} q J J𝒴) :
    IsGerbeOver J q F ↔ F.LocallyNonempty J𝒴 ∧ F.LocallyConnected J𝒴 := by
  constructor
  · intro hg
    exact ⟨(locallyNonempty_iff_locally_essSurj hq hF hJ𝒴).2 hg.locally_essSurj,
      (locallyConnected_iff_locally_full hq hF hJ𝒴).2 hg.locally_full⟩
  · rintro ⟨h2, h3⟩
    exact ⟨hq, Functor.IsFiberedInGroupoids.comp F q hF hq,
      (locallyNonempty_iff_locally_essSurj hq hF hJ𝒴).1 h2,
      (locallyConnected_iff_locally_full hq hF hJ𝒴).1 h3⟩

/-- Stacks 06P1 at the trivial factorization: for a 1-morphism `F : 𝒳 ⥤ 𝒴` of stacks in
groupoids over `(𝒞, J)` which is itself fibred in groupoids, `F` is a gerbe over the site
`(𝒴, J𝒴)` in the sense of Stacks 06NZ exactly when it satisfies the two local conditions of
Stacks 06P1 (2), that is exactly when `IsGerbeOver J q F`.

The `IsStackInGroupoids` conjunct of `IsGerbe` is free in both directions: it never contributes
to the two local conditions, and it is supplied by Stacks 06NX from the two stack hypotheses. -/
theorem Functor.isGerbe_iff_isGerbeOver
    (hp : Functor.IsStackInGroupoids.{max u₃ v₃} (F ⋙ q) J)
    (hq : Functor.IsStackInGroupoids.{max u₃ v₃} q J) (hF : F.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (hJ𝒴 : Functor.IsInheritedTopology.{max u₃ v₃} q J J𝒴) :
    F.IsGerbe.{max u₃ v₃} J𝒴 ↔ IsGerbeOver J q F := by
  rw [Functor.IsGerbe,
    isGerbeOver_iff_locallyNonempty_locallyConnected hq.isFiberedInGroupoids hF hJ𝒴]
  exact ⟨fun h => h.2, fun h =>
    ⟨Functor.isStackInGroupoids_of_isFiberedInGroupoids J J𝒴 (F ⋙ q) q F hp hq rfl hF hJ𝒴, h⟩⟩

/-- **Stacks 06P1**. Let `(𝒞, J)` be a site, let `q : 𝒴 ⥤ 𝒞` and `F ⋙ q : 𝒳 ⥤ 𝒞` be stacks in
groupoids over `𝒞` and let `J𝒴` be the topology on `𝒴` inherited from `(𝒞, J)`. Let
`F = a ⋙ F'` be a factorization of `F` through an equivalence `a` over `𝒞` with `F'` fibred in
groupoids — a factorization of exactly the kind Stacks 06N7 produces. Then clause (1) of
Stacks 06P1 — that `F'` is a gerbe over the site `(𝒴, J𝒴)` — holds exactly when clause (2) does,
that is exactly when `IsGerbeOver J q F`.

Since the right-hand side does not mention the factorization, this also says that clause (1) holds
for one such factorization exactly when it holds for every one, which is the source's parenthesis
"for some (equivalently any)".

The equivalence `a` is asked to be an equivalence over `𝒞`, as the source asks and as Stacks 06N7
delivers, not over `𝒴`: `CategoryTheory.isGerbeOver_iff_of_isEquivalenceOver`, the relative
Stacks 06P0, assumes the latter, and 06N7's factorization does not satisfy it — see
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Gerbe.BaseEquivalence`, which supplies the version used here.
-/
@[stacks 06P1]
theorem isGerbe_of_factorization_iff_isGerbeOver {𝒳' : Type u₄} [Category.{v₄} 𝒳']
    {F' : 𝒳' ⥤ 𝒴} {a : 𝒳 ⥤ 𝒳'} (ha : a ⋙ F' = F)
    (e : Functor.IsEquivalenceOver (F ⋙ q) (F' ⋙ q) a)
    (hp' : Functor.IsStackInGroupoids.{max u₃ v₃} (F' ⋙ q) J)
    (hq : Functor.IsStackInGroupoids.{max u₃ v₃} q J) (hF' : F'.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (hJ𝒴 : Functor.IsInheritedTopology.{max u₃ v₃} q J J𝒴) :
    F'.IsGerbe.{max u₃ v₃} J𝒴 ↔ IsGerbeOver J q F :=
  (Functor.isGerbe_iff_isGerbeOver hp' hq hF' hJ𝒴).trans
    (isGerbeOver_iff_of_isEquivalenceOver_base ha e).symm

end CategoryTheory
